# CODEOWNERS example. Every line below is commented out.
#
# Replace @your-org/maintainers with a real team (or user) in your
# organization, then uncomment the lines you want. GitHub requests a review
# from the listed owner when a pull request touches a matching path, and
# branch protection can require that review before merge.
#
# Docs: https://docs.github.com/repositories/managing-your-repositorys-settings-and-features/customizing-your-repository/about-code-owners

# Global: all files need a review from the maintainers team
# *                           @your-org/maintainers

# Kubernetes / Helm configs
# *.yaml                      @your-org/maintainers
# *.yml                       @your-org/maintainers
# k8s/                        @your-org/maintainers
# helm/                       @your-org/maintainers

# Terraform / OpenTofu
# *.tf                        @your-org/maintainers
# *.tfvars                    @your-org/maintainers
# infra/                      @your-org/maintainers

# CI/CD workflows
# .github/workflows/          @your-org/maintainers
# .github/actions/            @your-org/maintainers

# Dockerfiles
# Dockerfile*                 @your-org/maintainers
# docker-compose*.yml         @your-org/maintainers

# Security-sensitive files
# *.pem                       @your-org/maintainers
# *.crt                       @your-org/maintainers
